**Proposition 29.2 (what this particular common tuple preserves).**
For any $t,u\in\mathcal F_D$,

$$
J_Q(t)=J_Q(u)\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
      E_p(t)=E_p(u)\text{ for every }p\in Q.
\tag{GDB.117}
$$

Proof. Equality of fixed-slot tuples is equivalent to equality in each
slot. $\square$

Thus the kernel of this explicit tuple is the intersection of its
component kernels. This elementary common-source property imposes no
condition on an arbitrary optimal original code. Such a code need not
refine these chosen singleton maps or passively determine every factor;
its permitted late reply remains essential.

